<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daehan Pulp '96 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Daehan Pulp '96 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	 (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)	     (loss) 7,398     vs (gain) 455</p>
<p>    Net		     (loss)     9.19  vs (gain)   0.46</p>
<p>    Turnover			   233.35  vs	  223.71</p>
<p>    Loss/Profit before tax (loss)  9.88  vs (gain)   1.05</p>
<p>Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>				(preferred) none vs	    1.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Daehan Pulp Co Ltd said its share capital rose to 1.24 million common shares in 1996 from 920,000 the previous year, due to convertible bonds on overseas markets. A Daehan Pulp official blamed the 1996 loss on falling product prices.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
